			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843606">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Action</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> The Containment Procedure is crossed out.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The SCP itself are two books that are quantum entangled in the future. These books update as they are being written in the future. One of these books is a log of scientists trying to experiment with quantum entangling and details every single book that was entangled to the future and where to get them. This book gets taken, and the SCP Foundation has to find out who stole it using evidence and the other book, which was entangled in time by someone in the future warning them that they have to stop the thief from taking the book because society in the future will fall apart under one man's power.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The central narrative is from the SCP Foundation's perspective, tracking down an object that was taken from the inside and trying to find who did it before they escape. Basically a reverse heist.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Lots of twists and turns, a more story driven SCP that deals with slowly uncovering how someone stole the SCP as the Foundation tries to catch them before they escape.</p>

