<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Fantasy</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Appears as a deer or other local horned mammal trapped in a tree, fence, etc.</li>
<li>Often partially consumed or decomposing but the head typically remains lifelike</li>
<li>Individuals who come across it develop aggression towards whatever development is threatening the area and causing the SCP to manifest. They gain mild supernatural strength and endurance, as well as enhanced senses and become distressed if they are kept from accomplishing damage to the development</li>
<li>Those exposed retain an increased sense of connection with wilderness, but no powers or anger</li>
<li>The deer becomes fully skeletonized and loses anomalous properties if the ecosystem is damaged beyond repair or if the &quot;appointee&quot; is successful in neutralizing the development. Plants will rapidly cover the site of the development</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
*The world is fighting back against human and anomalous incursion but offers the chance for redemption to those lucky enough to receive its blessing<br />
*The foundation can use this phenomenon to its benefit, but only if they tread carefully<br />
*At first it's a threat to be neutralized, but through addenda, we learn that the foundation can exploit this for MTF operatives in wilderness scenarios.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
Incident log about a disastrous breach caused during the development of a new site at the hands of one of their own who came into contact with this SCP</p>
