<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> <strong>Yes</strong></p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> SCP Format</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
A Race of monkey like creatures that:<br />
*live in a corn field in southern Wisconsin that shows anomalous properties<br />
*have extremely long top teeth and claws<br />
*can use teeth and claws to extract the spine from a live human in seconds<br />
*uses the spine to craft a makeshift tail to be used to attract a mate<br />
*can not leave the cornfield without dying within minutes<br />
*has i diet consisting of only corn grown in that field and human blood<br />
*will die violently if fed anything else<br />
*help to exponentially increase the yield of the crop grown in the field<br />
*can mimic the crying and screams of a victims children to lure in to the field to be killed</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
Scp-xxxx are hairless monkey &quot;like&quot; creatures with large bulbous eyes and have elongated limbs. The creatures teeth and claws are also dis-proportionally elongated, with only the top portion of teeth being elongated in this way. Their spines are curved and distort wildly and they hunch over when on all four limbs. However, the spine can violently and grotesquely be straightened when threatened and standing in the up right position. Due to this violent transformation the spine is always exposed, being ripped through the skin during transformation.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong><br />
Scp-xxxx also posses the ability to mimic the sound of a lost child, crying and screaming for help. This has a psychological effect on most victims with children of their own as the cry's can mimic the victims offspring. It furthermore has a some what hypnotic effect on the victim, filling them with a misplaced sense of bravery and willingness to do what ever it takes to save the &quot;lost child&quot;.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I am looking for critiques and feedback on my writing. i am also seeking greenlight and any help building off this concept</p>
<p><a href="http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/thumperbunny27">http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/thumperbunny27</a></p>

